{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: factor x^2-1\nfactor x^2 - 1\n  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)\n  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)\n  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "factor x^2-1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["factor x^2-1"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "factor", "input": "x^2 - 1", "result": "(x - 1)*(x + 1)"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "normal_form", "passed": true, "text": "both sides have the same normal form"}], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "both sides have the same normal form over Q"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: factor x^2-1\nfactor x^2 - 1\n  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)\n  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)\n  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: factor x^2-1\nfactor x^2 - 1\n  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)\n  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)\n  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "factorise x^2-1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["factor x^2-1"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "factor", "input": "x^2 - 1", "result": "(x - 1)*(x + 1)"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "normal_form", "passed": true, "text": "both sides have the same normal form"}], "proof": {"kind": "symbolic", "text": "both sides have the same normal form over Q"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: factor x^2-1\nfactor x^2 - 1\n  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)\n  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)\n  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^3\n  ucas: symmetry it\nsymmetry of it:\n  odd: f(-x) = -f(x)\n  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "the centre of symmetry of x^3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^3", "symmetry it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "symmetry", "odd": "f(-x) = -f(x)", "proved_symbolically_parity_rules": "x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)", "headline": "symmetry of it:"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^3\n  ucas: symmetry it\nsymmetry of it:\n  odd: f(-x) = -f(x)\n  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)\n"}, "isError": false}}
